# Applies to the backend image build — docker-compose.yml builds it with the
# repo root as the context (backend/Dockerfile COPYs only backend/ and
# agent/aurum_agent). Everything heavy or secret that is not one of those two
# trees stays out of the context upload. The frontend image is unaffected: it
# builds from its own ./frontend context with its own .dockerignore.
#
# Patterns without a leading path only match at the context root, so the
# recursive **/ forms below are what actually guard the copied trees — a
# stray backend/.env or a __pycache__ left by a local test run must never
# ride into the image (the backend reads .env from its working directory
# at runtime, so a baked-in one would not even be dead weight).
.git
frontend
e2e
node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
